      "questionNumber": "07",
      "formatCode": "cq",
      "translations": {
        "bn": {
          "questionText": "$f(x)=\\frac{\\lnx}{{x}^{2}+1}......(i),$ g(x)=x^2+1....... (ii)$",
          "solutionText": null
        }
      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "ordinal": 1,
          "key": "A",
          "prompt": {
            "bn": "$\\int{(\\sin\\frac{x}{2}+\\cos\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}dx$ নির্ণয় কর।"
          },
          "solution": {
            "bn": "$\\int{(\\sin\\frac{x}{2}+\\cos\\frac{x}{2})}^{2}dx$\n$=\\int({\\sin}^{2}\\frac{x}{2}+{\\cos}^{2}\\frac{x}{2}+2\\sin\\frac{x}{2}\\cos\\frac{x}{2})dx$\n$=\\int(1+\\sin2\\cdot\\frac{x}{2})dx$\n$=\\int(1+\\sinx)dx$\n$=x-\\cosx+c$ [c একটি সমাকলন ধ্রুবক] (Ans.)"
          }
        },
        {
          "ordinal": 2,
          "key": "B",
          "prompt": {
            "bn": "(i) বক্ররেখার $x=2$ বিন্দুতে ম্পর্শকের সমীকরণ নির্ণয় কর।"
          },
          "solution": {
            "bn": "ধরি, $y=f(x)=\\frac{\\lnx}{{x}^{2}+1}$\n${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)\\frac{d}{dx}(\\lnx)-\\lnx\\frac{d}{dx}({x}^{2}+1)}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}$\n$=\\frac{({x}^{2}+1)\\frac{1}{x}-\\lnx\\cdot2x}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}$\n$=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2}\\lnx}{x}$\n$=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2}\\lnx}{x{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}$\n$x=2$ বিन्দুতে ${f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{{2}^{2}+1-2\\times{2}^{2}\\times\\ln2}{2{({2}^{2}+1)}^{2}}=\\frac{5-8\\ln2}{50}$\n$x=2$ হলে $y=\\frac{\\ln2}{{2}^{2}+1}=\\frac{\\ln2}{5}$\n$(2,\\frac{\\ln2}{5})$ বিন্দুতে স্পর্শকের সমীকরণ, \n$y-\\frac{\\ln2}{5}=\\frac{5-8\\ln2}{50}(x-2)$\nবা, $50y-10\\ln2=(5-8\\ln2)x-10+16\\ln2$\n$∴(5-8\\ln2)x-50y-10+26\\ln2=0\\text{ (Ans.) }$"
          }
        },
        {
          "ordinal": 3,
          "key": "C",
          "prompt": {
            "bn": "${\\int}_{0}^{1}f(x).g(x)dx$ এর মান নির্ণয় কর।"
          },
          "solution": {
            "bn": "$\\begin{matrix} & {\\int}_{0}^{1}f(x)\\cdotg(x)dx={\\int}_{0}^{1}\\frac{\\lnx}{{x}^{2}+1}({x}^{2}+1)dx\\\\ & ={\\int}_{0}^{1}\\lnxdx\\\\ & ∴\\int\\lnxdx=\\lnx\\intdx-\\int[\\frac{d}{dx}(\\lnx)\\intdx]dx\\\\ & =x\\lnx-\\int\\frac{1}{x}\\cdotxdx\\\\ & =x\\lnx-x+c\\\\ & ∴{\\int}_{0}^{1}f(x)g(x)dx=[x\\lnx-x{]}_{0}^{1}\\\\ & =(0-1)-0=-1\\text{ (Ans.) }\\\\ & \\end{matrix}$"
          }
        }
      ],
